JPA offers three strategies for entity inheritance mapping:

1. **SINGLE_TABLE** (default): One table for all entities in the hierarchy, with a discriminator column

```java
@Entity
@Inheritance(strategy = InheritanceType.SINGLE_TABLE)
@DiscriminatorColumn(name = "type")
public abstract class Payment { ... }

@Entity
@DiscriminatorValue("CC")
public class CreditCardPayment extends Payment { ... }
```

2. **JOINED**: Separate tables for each class, joined when querying

```java
@Entity
@Inheritance(strategy = InheritanceType.JOINED)
public abstract class Payment { ... }
```

3. **TABLE_PER_CLASS**: Separate tables for each concrete class with all fields

```java
@Entity
@Inheritance(strategy = InheritanceType.TABLE_PER_CLASS)
public abstract class Payment { ... }
```

